gth final group, and state whether the line-break-split fragment \'US39\' + NEWLINE + \'OBAK\' becomes detectable under the corrected pattern.\\n - CLS-PII-ADDRESS-001 over-extended from 293 to 364, swallowing \'\\\\nSocial Security Number\'. Confirm that the trailing character class includes \\\\s and specify the corrected boundary rule (semantic address must terminate at the last address token before a newline+label boundary), with corrected pattern.\\n - CLS-PHI-MED-ID-001 produced zero matches for \'HI-902849102-B\' because of the MC|MEM|PAT|REC prefix requirement. Confirm.\\n\\n(C) NEW CLASSIFIERS \\u2014 full proposed definitions (id, category, pattern, priority, confidence, confidence_threshold, validator, test cases) for:\\n 1. CLS-PII-USERNAME-001 \\u2014 system account username. Note proposed confidence ~0.75 sits BELOW the existing PII confidence floor of 0.85; specify the stricter separator/context-anchored pattern that would justify raising it to >=0.85 or state explicitly that Human Admin must grant a floor exception. Must match \'mavance_admin\' at [83,96] and avoid matching email local-parts already covered, URLs, and ordinary words.\\n 2. CLS-PHI-INSURANCE-MEMBER-ID-001 \\u2014 health insurance member/identifier. Must match \'HI-902849102-B\' at [403,417]. Specify how it coexists with existing CLS-PHI-MED-ID-001 (priority order, overlap resolution expectations).\\n\\n(D) SCHEMA EXTENSIONS required: exact JSON paths to add USERNAME under PII.IDENTIFIER.types and HEALTH_INSURANCE_MEMBER_ID under PHI.MEDICAL_IDENTIFIER.types, plus any new type needed for payment card if not already present.\\n\\n(E) REGRESSION REQUIREMENTS: the four documents processed so far (New_Test_File.pdf, Marcus Vance System Account Record.pdf, test_file.pdf, plus the earlier New_Test_File.pdf variant) must be re-run; state expected span-count deltas per document under rev-002, and list any span that must NOT change (e.g., person name, email, phone, passport, IP, SSN offsets must remain stable).\\n\\n(F) RELEASE/MIRROR PLAN: version bump (1.0.0 -> 1.1.0), revision id rev-002, status PINNED, integrity hash recomputation, history entry type (ADD_CLASSIFIERS + MODIFY_CLASSIFIERS), the exact mirror file paths that must be synced atomically and content-equivalent, and the detector re-pin sequence.\\n\\n(G) RISK & ROLLBACK: false-positive risks per change, precision/recall tradeoffs, and rollback procedure to rev-001.\\n\\nReturn the complete draft specification in a structured, copy-ready form suitable for Human Admin review and sign-off. Do not activate anything.", "mode": "Fulfill"}}'}
