mber ID: HI-902849102-B on file\\" -> confirm no match, print None.\\n- new_ins = r\'\\\\b[A-Z]{2}-\\\\d{9}-[A-Z]\\\\b\' on the same string -> print span and matched text; then compute offset of \'HI-902849102-B\' via s.find() and confirm whether span == (11,25).\\n\\nPART 5 \\u2014 USERNAME.\\nS = \\"Patient record for Marcus Vance. Account: mavance_admin assigned; contact marcus.vance@example.com and see https://portal.example.com/mavance_admin and the word administrator here.\\"\\n- print S.index(\'mavance_admin\') to check the [83,96] claim.\\n- loose = r\'(?<![A-Za-z0-9._%+\\\\-])[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9._\\\\-]{2,31}(?![A-Za-z0-9.@])\' -> print ALL matches with spans; label which are false positives.\\n- strict_context = r\'(?<=Account: )[a-z][a-z0-9._\\\\-]{2,31}(?=\\\\s|;|,|$)\' -> print matches with spans; confirm it yields only \'mavance_admin\' at (83,96) and ignores the email local part, the URL path segment, and \'administrator\'.\\n\\nPART 1 re-confirm \\u2014 print Luhn digit-sum breakdown for \'4532891043219081\' to prove the fail, plus Luhn for a known-valid Visa test number \'4111111111111111\' and \'4012888888881881\'.\\n\\nPrint everything explicitly with prints, no bare expression tuples.", "origin": [{"tool": "orchestrator_supervisor_agent", "instantiation_index": 1}, {"tool": "classification_detection_agent", "instantiation_index": 1}, {"tool": "openai_code_interpreter", "instantiation_index": 2}], "origin_str": "orchestrator_supervisor_agent.classification_detection_agent.openai_code_interpreter-02"}}'}
