2026-10-19 12:40:24 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-19 12:40:24 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent'], 'text': 'result from classification_detection_agent\n## DRAFT — rev-002 CHANGE REQUEST SPECIFICATION\n**Status: NON-ACTIVATING PROPOSAL ONLY — nothing pinned, mutated, or activated.**\nPrepared by: PII/PHI Span Detection agent (detection logic executed deterministically in `openai_code_interpreter`; verbatim definitions served read-only by `master_classifier_repository_agent`).\nTarget: `master_data_classifiers/ruleset.json` (currently `rev-001`, `ruleset_version` 1.0.0, status PINNED, `integrity_hash: sha256-rev1-master-data-classifiers-pinned`).\n\n> **Three corrections to the premises in the change request, established from the pinned source and from run evidence. These must be settled before sign-off:**\n> 1. **There is no "global PII confidence floor of 0.85" in rev-001.** rev-001 defines *only* per-classifier `confidence_threshold` values; the lowest PII value is **0.80** (`CLS-PII-NAME-001`, NER) and the lowest PHI value is **0.85** (`CLS-PHI-CONDITION-001`). No aggregate/floor field exists. So a 0.75 username would not violate a field that does not exist — but it *would* be below every existing regex PII threshold (min regex PII = 0.85). Recommendation below still raises it to ≥0.85 on precision grounds, and no "floor exception" is technically required unless Admin *chooses* to codify a global floor as a new schema field.\n> 2. **rev-001 has no `validators`, no `match_strategy`, and no per-match `confidence` field.** Every validator/Luhn/match-strategy element in this draft is therefore a **schema extension**, not a field edit. The `priority`/`confidence_threshold`/`mask_token` fields do exist.\n> 3. **`4532-8910-4321-9081` FAILS the Luhn check** (digit-sum 72, 72 mod 10 = 2). A hard Luhn gate would *suppress the very true positive this change is meant to catch*. A soft-fail confidence tier is specified in (B1) — **Admin decision required.**\n\n---\n\n## (A) CURRENT PINNED DEFINITIONS — verbatim from rev-001\n\nPatterns below are shown in human-readable (unescaped) form; **in the file they carry one level of JSON escaping** (`\\\\b`, `\\\\d`, …). Byte-exact quoting must be taken from `master_data_classifiers/ruleset.json`.\n\n### A1. `CLS-PII-CC-001` — Credit Card Number\n```json\n{\n  "classifier_id": "CLS-PII-CC-001",\n  "category": "PII.FINANCIAL.CREDIT_CARD",\n  "type": "regex",\n  "pattern": "\\\\b(?:4\\\\d{3}|5[1-5]\\\\d{2}|6011|3[47]\\\\d{2})[- ]?\\\\d{4}[- ]?\\\\d{4}[- ]?\\\\d{4}\\\\b|\\\\b\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{4}\\\\b",\n  "confidence_threshold": 0.95,\n  "priority": 1,\n  "mask_token": "[CREDIT_CARD]",\n  "validators": "ABSENT",\n  "match_strategy": "ABSENT"\n}\n```\n\n### A2. `CLS-PII-IBAN-001` — Bank Account (IBAN)\n```json\n{\n  "classifier_id": "CLS-PII-IBAN-001",\n  "category": "PII.FINANCIAL.BANK_ACCOUNT",\n  "type": "regex",\n  "pattern": "\\\\b[A-Z]{2}\\\\d{2}(?:\\\\s?[A-Z0-9]{4}){3,7}\\\\b",\n  "confidence_threshold": 0.90,\n  "priority": 2,\n  "mask_token": "[BANK_ACCOUNT]",\n  "validators": "ABSENT",\n  "match_strategy": "ABSENT"\n}\n```\nNote: named "IBAN" but bound to `PII.FINANCIAL.BANK_ACCOUNT` / `[BANK_ACCOUNT]`; the enum member `PII.FINANCIAL.IBAN` is targeted by **no** classifier.\n\n### A3. `CLS-PII-ADDRESS-001` — Residential / Work Street Address\n```json\n{\n  "classifier_id": "CLS-PII-ADDRESS-001",\n  "category": "PII.LOCATION.STREET_ADDRESS",\n  "type": "regex",\n  "pattern": "\\\\b\\\\d{1,5}\\\\s+[A-Za-z0-9\\\\s.,]+(?:Terrace|Street|St|Avenue|Ave|Road|Rd|Boulevard|Blvd|Way|Lane|Ln|Drive|Dr)(?:[A-Za-z0-9\\\\s.,#]+)?(?:,\\\\s+[A-Za-z\\\\s]+,\\\\s+[A-Z]{2}\\\\s+\\\\d{5}(?:-\\\\d{4})?)?\\\\b",\n  "confidence_threshold": 0.85,\n  "priority": 4,\n  "mask_token": "[STREET_ADDRESS]",\n  "validators": "ABSENT",\n  "match_strategy": "ABSENT"\n}\n```\n\n### A4. `CLS-PHI-MED-ID-001` — Medical Case Ref / Patient Member ID\n```json\n{\n  "classifier_id": "CLS-PHI-MED-ID-001",\n  "category": "PHI.MEDICAL_IDENTIFIER",\n  "type": "regex",\n  "pattern": "\\\\b(?:MC|MEM|PAT|REC)-[A-Za-z0-9-]{4,15}\\\\b",\n  "confidence_threshold": 0.90,\n  "priority": 2,\n  "mask_token": "[MEDICAL_ID]",\n  "validators": "ABSENT",\n  "match_strategy": "ABSENT"\n}\n```\nNote: `category` has **no type suffix**, so it binds to neither `PATIENT_ID` nor `MEDICAL_CASE_REF`.\n\n### A5. Current category enum trees (verbatim)\n```\nPII\n├── PERSON_NAME         (no types array — leaf)\n├── IDENTIFIER          types: ["SSN", "NATIONAL_ID", "PASSPORT", "DRIVERS_LICENSE"]\n├── CONTACT             types: ["EMAIL", "PHONE_NUMBER"]\n├── LOCATION            types: ["STREET_ADDRESS", "IP_ADDRESS"]\n├── FINANCIAL           types: ["CREDIT_CARD", "BANK_ACCOUNT", "IBAN", "CVV"]\n└── DEMOGRAPHIC         types: ["DATE_OF_BIRTH"]\n\nPHI\n├── MEDICAL_IDENTIFIER  types: ["PATIENT_ID", "MEDICAL_CASE_REF"]\n└── HEALTH_DATA         types: ["ALLERGY", "CONDITION", "PRESCRIPTION", "CLINICAL_NOTE"]\n```\nrev-001 inventory: **13 classifiers**; history has 1 entry (`CREATE_INITIAL_PINNED_REVISION`, added 13, modified 0, removed 0); `pending_admin_review: []`.\n\n---\n\n## (B) EVIDENCE OF DEFECTS — measured, not asserted\n\nAll results below were produced by executing the patterns against the exact evidence strings.\n\n### B1. `CLS-PII-CC-001` — 0 matches on `test_file.pdf` (3 occurrences of the card)\n**Root cause confirmed: the separator class `[- ]?` admits exactly one character, and only hyphen or space — never a newline, and never two whitespace chars.**\n\n| Test input | rev-001 pattern | Corrected pattern |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Visa 4532-\\n8910-4321-9081` | **no match** | match `[5,25]` |\n| `4532-8910-4321-9081` | match `[0,19]` | match `[0,19]` |\n| `4532-\\n8910-\\n4321-9081` | **no match** | match `[0,21]` |\n| `4532  8910  4321  9081` (double spaces) | **no match** | match |\n| `4532-\\n\\n8910-4321-9081` (blank line) | no match | **no match** (guard holds) |\n| `order 1234\\n5678\\n9012` (12 digits) | no match | no match |\n| `ref 2026\\n1016` (date-like) | no match | no match |\n| `3782 822463 10005` (Amex 4-6-5, 15 digit) | no match | **no match — out of scope, see risk R1** |\n\n**Corrected separator class requirement:** must accept `hyphen`, spaces/tabs (runs of any length), and **at most one newline** per separator, but must **not** allow a blank line (which would let a match bridge two unrelated paragraphs).\n\n**Corrected pattern (validated):**\n```json\n"pattern": "\\\\b(?:\\\\d{4}(?:[ \\\\t\\\\-]*\\\\n?[ \\\\t\\\\-]*)){3}\\\\d{4}\\\\b"\n```\nHuman-readable: `\\b(?:\\d{4}(?:[ \\t\\-]*\\n?[ \\t\\-]*)){3}\\d{4}\\b`\n\n**Luhn post-validator (new `validators` block) — and the conflict:**\n```\nluhn(digits):\n  digits = [int(c) for c in re.sub(r\'\\D\',\'\',match)]\n  return (sum(digits[-1::-2]) + sum(sum(divmod(2*d,10)) for d in digits[-2::-2])) % 10 == 0\n```\n- `4111111111111111` → **pass** (digit-sum 30)\n- `4012888888881881` → **pass** (digit-sum 90)\n- `4532891043219081` (**the card actually present in `test_file.pdf`**) → **FAIL** (digit-sum 72)\n\n**Therefore a hard Luhn gate is unsafe on the current corpus.** Proposed **two-tier soft-fail** design (Admin must select Option 1 or 2):\n\n```json\n"validators": [\n  { "id": "luhn_mod10", "type": "checksum", "algorithm": "LUHN",\n    "on_pass": { "confidence": 0.99, "status": "LUHN_PASS" },\n    "on_fail": { "confidence": 0.86, "status": "LUHN_FAIL", "emit_metadata": true } }\n],\n"confidence_threshold": 0.85\n```\n- **Option 1 (recommended):** `confidence_threshold: 0.85`, base confidence 0.88, Luhn-pass 0.99, Luhn-fail 0.86 → the document\'s card is detected **and** flagged `validator_status: LUHN_FAIL` for reviewer attention.\n- **Option 2 (strict precision):** `confidence_threshold: 0.95`, Luhn-fail suppressed → **the defect is NOT fixed for `test_file.pdf`**; would require the Human Admin to accept a known false negative.\n\n### B2. `CLS-PII-IBAN-001` — truncation of the final 2-char group\n**Root cause confirmed: `(?:\\s?[A-Z0-9]{4}){3,7}` forces every group to be exactly 4 chars, so a short final group can never be captured.**\n\n| Test input | rev-001 pattern | Corrected pattern |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Account: US39 OBAK 0123 4567 8901 23 (ref)` | match span **(9,33)** = `US39 OBAK 0123 4567 8901` — ends at 33, leaving ` 23` behind | match span **(9,36)** = `US39 OBAK 0123 4567 8901 23` |\n| `US39\\nOBAK 0123 4567 8901 23` | no match (`\\s?`+`{4}` interaction) | match `[0,27]` |\n| space-only variant on the newline input | no match | — (proves the newline must be admitted) |\n| `US39\\n\\nOBAK 0123` | no match | **no match** (blank-line guard) |\n| `The US39 code` / `AB12` | no match | no match |\n\nThis reproduces the reported `[439,463]` truncation exactly (relative span 9→33, length 24; in the document `[439,463]`).\n\n**Corrected pattern (validated), variable-length final group + bounded newline:**\n```json\n"pattern": "\\\\b[A-Z]{2}\\\\d{2}(?:[ \\\\t]*\\\\n?[ \\\\t]*[A-Z0-9]{4}){1,7}(?:[ \\\\t]*\\\\n?[ \\\\t]*[A-Z0-9]{1,3})?\\\\b"\n```\nHuman-readable: `\\b[A-Z]{2}\\d{2}(?:[ \\t]*\\n?[ \\t]*[A-Z0-9]{4}){1,7}(?:[ \\t]*\\n?[ \\t]*[A-Z0-9]{1,3})?\\b`\nAdd post-filter `strip_separators` → assert cleaned alnum length in **10..34** (IBAN max) before emitting.\n\n**Does `\'US39\' + NEWLINE + \'OBAK\'` become detectable? YES** under the corrected pattern — **only because** the separator is `[ \\t]*\\n?[ \\t]*` rather than `[ ]?` (the space-only variant returns **no match**). This is a direct dependency of the fix: do **not** narrow the corrected separator to a single space.\n\n### B3. `CLS-PII-ADDRESS-001` — over-extension swallowing `\\nSocial Security Number`\n**Root cause confirmed: the trailing optional class `[A-Za-z0-9\\s.,#]+` contains `\\s`, so it consumes newlines, and it contains digits, so it consumes the start of the SSN line.**\n\n| Test input | rev-001 pattern | Corrected pattern |\n|---|---|---|\n| `1200 Market Street Suite 400\\nSocial Security Number 123-45-6789` | span **(0,55)**, captured `\'1200 Market Street Suite 400\\nSocial Security Number 123\'` — **crosses the newline into the label and into the SSN digits** | span **(0,28)** = `\'1200 Market Street Suite 400\'`, stops **before** the newline |\n| `742 Evergreen Terrace, Springfield, IL 62704\\nPhone: 555-0100` | — | `\'742 Evergreen Terrace, Springfield, IL 62704\'` (ZIP retained, stops at newline) |\n| `500 West 5th Ave\\nNew York` | — | `\'500 West 5th Ave\'` |\n| `No address here at all` | — | no match |\n\n**Corrected boundary rule:** the address body (number, street tokens, street-type suffix, secondary unit) may use **`[ \\t]` only — never `\\s`**, and may contain no more than 6 street tokens; the semantic address terminates at the last address token before any newline, so a `\\n` + label boundary can never be entered. Plus the `Suite|Ste|Unit|Apt|Bldg|Floor|Fl` secondary-unit group and the `, City, ST ZIP(+4)` group become explicit optional groups with the **same** `[ \\t]`-only discipline.\n\n**Corrected pattern (validated):**\n```json\n"pattern": "\\\\b\\\\d{1,5}[ \\\\t]+(?:[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9.\\\\-#]*[ \\\\t]+){0,6}(?:Terrace|Street|St|Avenue|Ave|Road|Rd|Boulevard|Blvd|Way|Lane|Ln|Drive|Dr)\\\\b(?:[ \\\\t]*,[ \\\\t]*(?:Suite|Ste|Unit|Apt|Bldg|Floor|Fl)[ \\\\t]*#?[0-9A-Za-z-]+|[ \\\\t]+(?:Suite|Ste|Unit|Apt|Bldg|Floor|Fl)[ \\\\t]*#?[0-9A-Za-z-]+)?(?:,[ \\\\t]+[A-Za-z .]+,[ \\\\t]+[A-Z]{2}[ \\\\t]+\\\\d{5}(?:-\\\\d{4})?)?"\n```\nAdd post-filter `truncate_at_newline`: if a match still contains `\\n` (defensive), trim to the last `[ \\t]`-delimited token before it and re-check it ends on an address token.\n\n### B4. `CLS-PHI-MED-ID-001` — zero matches for `HI-902849102-B`\n**Confirmed.** `\\b(?:MC|MEM|PAT|REC)-[A-Za-z0-9-]{4,15}\\b` returns **no match** against `Member ID: HI-902849102-B on file`. The anchor set `MC|MEM|PAT|REC` does not include `HI`, and the trailing `\\b` would not accommodate the `-B` suffix pattern as a distinct segment. The correct fix is **not** to add `HI` to `MED-ID` (that would conflate a case ref with an insurance member ID) but to add a distinct classifier — see (C2). Additionally the existing classifier\'s body `[A-Za-z0-9-]{4,15}` is too loose (accepts `REC-1234`), so a MED-ID tightening is proposed separately in (B5).\n\n### B5. Optional MED-ID tightening (recommended, low risk)\n`"pattern": "\\\\b(?:MC|MEM|PAT|REC)-\\\\d{6,12}(?:-[A-Z0-9]{1,2})?\\\\b"` — keeps existing true positives (`REC-2026-0042` style needs the hyphen branch, so Admin should confirm the corpus before adopting). **If unsure, leave `CLS-PHI-MED-ID-001` pattern untouched in rev-002** and only add the insurance classifier; the spec below marks this optional.\n\n---\n\n## (C) NEW CLASSIFIERS\n\n### C1. `CLS-PII-USERNAME-001` — system account username\n\n**Precision problem with the generic pattern:** a naive `(?<![A-Za-z0-9._%+\\-])[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9._\\-]{2,31}(?![A-Za-z0-9.@])` **over-matches ordinary words, email local-parts and URL path segments** — measured false positives on the sentence *"…contact marcus.vance@example.com and see https://portal.example.com/mavance_admin and administrator"*.\n\n**Context-anchored pattern that justifies ≥0.85 (validated).** Note this is a **capture-group** classifier: the emitted span is **group 1**, not group 0 (group 0 includes the `Account:` label):\n```json\n{\n  "classifier_id": "CLS-PII-USERNAME-001",\n  "category": "PII.IDENTIFIER.USERNAME",\n  "type": "regex",\n  "pattern": "(?:\\\\b(?:Account Name|Username|Account|Login|User)[ \\\\t]*:[ \\\\t]*)([a-z][a-z0-9._\\\\-]{2,31})(?![A-Za-z0-9.@\\\\-])",\n  "span_group": 1,\n  "confidence": 0.86,\n  "confidence_threshold": 0.85,\n  "priority": 3,\n  "mask_token": "[USERNAME]",\n  "validators": [\n    { "id": "not_email_localpart", "type": "negative_lookahead_guard", "spec": "reject if followed by \'@\' or if preceded by an email/URL token boundary" },\n    { "id": "label_anchor_required", "type": "context_anchor", "spec": "account|username|login|user label with colon" }\n  ]\n}\n```\nMeasured behaviour:\n\n| Input | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `Account: mavance_admin assigned; contact marcus.vance@example.com and see https://portal.example.com/mavance_admin and administrator` | **only** `mavance_admin`, group-1 span `(9,22)`; email, URL path and `administrator` **not** matched |\n| `Username: m.vance` | `m.vance` `(10,17)` |\n| `mavance_admin` (no label) | **no match** — proves context anchoring |\n| `user marcus.vance@example.com` | **no match** |\n| `Account mavance_admin` (no colon) | **no match** |\n\nIn the document\'s own text the same construct yields **`mavance_admin` at `[83,96]`** (the synthetic probe string yields 9–22 purely because of a shorter prefix).\n\n**Floor question, resolved:** (i) rev-001 has no global floor, so no *technical* exception is needed; (ii) the proposed **0.86 / threshold 0.85 is justified by the label anchoring** (label + colon is a mandatory, non-optional lookbehind, which is what makes the difference between ~0.75 naive precision and ≥0.85); (iii) **Admin decision D-3:** either accept 0.86/0.85 as specified, **or** if Admin elects to codify a *global PII floor = 0.85* as a new schema field, this classifier already complies. **No 0.75 variant is proposed.**\n**Implementation constraint:** Python `re` requires fixed-width look-behind, and `(?:Account|Username|User)` is variable width — **the consuming-prefix + `span_group: 1` form above is mandatory**; a `(?<=…)` lookbehind form raises `error: look-behind requires fixed-width pattern` (observed).\n\n### C2. `CLS-PHI-INSURANCE-MEMBER-ID-001` — health insurance member identifier\n```json\n{\n  "classifier_id": "CLS-PHI-INSURANCE-MEMBER-ID-001",\n  "category": "PHI.MEDICAL_IDENTIFIER.HEALTH_INSURANCE_MEMBER_ID",\n  "type": "regex",\n  "pattern": "\\\\b[A-Z]{2}-\\\\d{9}-[A-Z]\\\\b",\n  "confidence": 0.93,\n  "confidence_threshold": 0.90,\n  "priority": 2,\n  "mask_token": "[INSURANCE_MEMBER_ID]",\n  "validators": [\n    { "id": "issuer_prefix_allowlist", "type": "dictionary_and_heuristic",\n      "spec": "2-char alpha payer/plan prefix (HI, BC, AH, UN, …); Admin to confirm the closed list" },\n    { "id": "segment_shape", "type": "heuristic", "spec": "exactly 9 numeric digits then one check alpha" }\n  ]\n}\n```\nMeasured behaviour: `Member ID: HI-902849102-B on file` → match **`(11,25)`** = `HI-902849102-B`, length **14** — i.e. **`[403,417]` in the document**, exactly as required. `AB-123456789-X` → match. `not an id HI-90284-B` → no match.\n\n**Coexistence with `CLS-PHI-MED-ID-001`:**\n- **Priority:** both `priority: 2`. This is safe **by construction** because the prefix alphabets are **disjoint** (`HI` vs `MC|MEM|PAT|REC`), so the two patterns cannot overlap on the same character range.\n- **Overlap-resolution expectation: zero collisions on the current corpus** (expected — must be asserted by test, not assumed).\n- **If a future revision breaks disjointness**, the global resolver (see §H, which rev-002 must define because rev-001 has no `match_strategy`) decides: start offset ascending → longest match descending → priority ascending → confidence descending → keep highest-ranked non-overlapping span. Under that rule a 14-char `HI-…` span outranks any shorter `MED-ID` fragment.\n- **Both must never emit on the same span.** Add a regression assertion `Σ INS spans ∩ Σ MED-ID spans = ∅`.\n\n---\n\n## (D) SCHEMA EXTENSIONS\n\n| # | Exact JSON path | Change | Value |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| D-1 | `category_enums.PII.IDENTIFIER.types` | append | `"USERNAME"` → `["SSN","NATIONAL_ID","PASSPORT","DRIVERS_LICENSE","USERNAME"]` |\n| D-2 | `category_enums.PHI.MEDICAL_IDENTIFIER.types` | append | `"HEALTH_INSURANCE_MEMBER_ID"` → `["PATIENT_ID","MEDICAL_CASE_REF","HEALTH_INSURANCE_MEMBER_ID"]` |\n| D-3 | `category_enums.PII.FINANCIAL.types` | **no change needed** | `"CREDIT_CARD"` already present; `"IBAN"` already present (currently unused). *No new payment-card type is required.* |\n| D-4 | `classifiers[].validators` | **new field** (absent in rev-001) | array of `{id,type,algorithm,on_pass,on_fail}` |\n| D-5 | `classifiers[].confidence` | **new field** (absent in rev-001; only `confidence_threshold` exists) | static base confidence **overridden per-match by validators** |\n| D-6 | `classifiers[].span_group` | **new field** | integer, default `0`; required `1` for `CLS-PII-USERNAME-001` |\n| D-7 | `match_strategy` (top level) | **new field** (absent in rev-001) | see §H |\n| D-8 | `classifiers[].category` for `CLS-PHI-MED-ID-001` | **optional** normalization | `"PHI.MEDICAL_IDENTIFIER"` → `"PHI.MEDICAL_IDENTIFIER.MEDICAL_CASE_REF"` (no behavioural change; makes the binding enum-legal) |\n| D-9 | `classifiers[].category` for `CLS-PII-IBAN-001` | **optional** normalization | `PII.FINANCIAL.BANK_ACCOUNT`/[BANK_ACCOUNT] → `PII.FINANCIAL.IBAN`/[IBAN], activating the dormant enum member. **Admin decision D-4.** |\n\n---\n\n## (H) `match_strategy` block to be added (rev-001 has none)\n```json\n"match_strategy": {\n  "overlap_resolution": "deterministic",\n  "order": ["start_offset:asc", "match_length:desc", "priority:asc", "confidence:desc", "classifier_id:asc"],\n  "on_tie": "keep_first",\n  "dedupe": "identical_start_end_category",\n  "span_source": "span_group_if_defined_else_full_match"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## (E) REGRESSION REQUIREMENTS\n\n**Disambiguation prerequisite:** the corpus is listed as *four* documents but the name `New_Test_File.pdf` appears twice ("plus the earlier New_Test_File.pdf variant"). **Admin must supply a distinct identifier (sha256 or mtime) per file**, otherwise the delta table below cannot be bound to a specific artefact.\n\n### E1. Expected span-count / offset deltas under rev-002\n| Document | Classifier | rev-001 | rev-002 | Delta | Basis |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `test_file.pdf` | `CLS-PII-CC-001` | **0** | **3** | **+3** | three occurrences of `4532-\\n8910-4321-9081`; each span 20 chars |\n| `test_file.pdf` | `CLS-PII-IBAN-001` | 1 @ `[439,463]` | **1 @ `[439,466]`** | count **0**, end offset **+3** (final group ` 23` recovered) | measured relative span 9→36 vs 9→33 |\n| `test_file.pdf` | `CLS-PII-ADDRESS-001` | 1, end **364** | 1, end **≈341** | count **0**, end offset **−23** (`\\nSocial Security Number`) | 364 − len("\\nSocial Security Number") = 341; ±1 if a trailing space is trimmed — **confirm on re-run** |\n| `test_file.pdf` | `CLS-PHI-INSURANCE-MEMBER-ID-001` | 0 (n/a) | **1 @ `[403,417]`** | **+1** | new classifier; measured span length 14 |\n| `test_file.pdf` | `CLS-PHI-MED-ID-001` | 0 | 0 | 0 | confirmed defect; unchanged unless §B5 adopted |\n| `test_file.pdf` | `CLS-PII-USERNAME-001` | 0 (n/a) | **0 expected** | 0 | no `Account:`/`Username:` label evidence in this file |\n| `Marcus Vance System Account Record.pdf` | `CLS-PII-USERNAME-001` | 0 (n/a) | **1 @ `[83,96]`** | **+1** | required match |\n| `Marcus Vance System Account Record.pdf` | all other 15 | unchanged | unchanged | **0** | no CC/IBAN/address/insurance evidence reported |\n| `New_Test_File.pdf` (current) | all | baseline | baseline | **0 expected** | no defect evidence attributed to this file — **delta must be measured, not assumed** |\n| `New_Test_File.pdf` (earlier variant) | all | baseline | baseline | **0 expected** | as above; may itself contain a CC/IBAN — **must be fingerprinted** |\n\nTotals: rev-001 **13** classifiers → rev-002 **15**; document-level detection totals per file must be recomputed and recorded in `detection_metadata` (`total_detections`, `counts_per_category`).\n\n### E2. Spans that must **NOT** change (offset-and-length equality assertions)\nAcross **all four** documents, the following must be byte-identical before/after:\n- `CLS-PII-NAME-001` — person name spans (e.g. `Marcus Vance`), **never** inside a username span.\n- `CLS-PII-EMAIL-001` — e.g. `marcus.vance@example.com` `[..]`; the new username classifier **must not** clip or duplicate it (assert no username span intersects an email span).\n- `CLS-PII-SSN-001` — e.g. `123-45-6789`; assert the address span\'s new end (≈341) is still `<` the SSN start, and that the SSN offset is **unchanged** (rev-001\'s over-extension stopped *before* the digits, so SSN was already stable — this must be proven, not assumed).\n- `CLS-PII-PHONE-001`, `CLS-PII-PASSPORT-001`, `CLS-PII-IP-001`, `CLS-PII-DOB-001`, `CLS-PII-DL-001`, `CLS-PHI-CONDITION-001` — all unchanged.\n- `priority`/`confidence_threshold` of the **9 untouched** classifiers unchanged.\n\n### E3. Required assertions (golden-corpus harness)\n1. `count(CLS-PII-CC-001, test_file.pdf) == 3` and each matched text, after newline-stripping, == `4532891043219081`.\n2. `span(CLS-PII-IBAN-001)` end == 466 and matched text endswith `23`.\n3. `"\\n" not in span(CLS-PII-ADDRESS-001)`; end `<` index of the `Social` label; end `<` SSN start.\n4. `span(CLS-PHI-INSURANCE-MEMBER-ID-001) == [403,417]`; `text == "HI-902849102-B"`.\n5. `span(CLS-PII-USERNAME-001) == [83,96]` on the Marcus Vance record; `text == "mavance_admin"`.\n6. `Σ INS spans ∩ Σ MED-ID spans == ∅`.\n7. `Σ USERNAME spans ∩ Σ EMAIL spans == ∅`; `Σ USERNAME spans ∩ Σ (URL host/path) == ∅`.\n8. Negative corpus: `administrator`, `The US39 code`, `AB12`, `1234\\n5678\\n9012`, `4532-\\n\\n8910-4321-9081`, `Account mavance_admin` → **no** matches.\n\n---\n\n## (F) RELEASE / MIRROR PLAN (proposal — requires Human Admin approval to execute)\n\n| Step | Action |\n|---|---|\n| F1 | `ruleset_version`: **1.0.0 → 1.1.0** (minor: additive classifiers + backwards-compatible pattern corrections; no category removals) |\n| F2 | `metadata.revision`: `1 → 2`; `active_revision_id`: `rev-001 → **rev-002**` |\n| F3 | `status`: `PINNED` (only after Admin token) |\n| F4 | `metadata.approval_actor` / `approval_token` / `approval_timestamp` **new values — must not reuse** `ADMIN-ROOT-001` / `AUTH-TOKEN-ADMIN-REV1-APPROVED-20261016-ROOT` |\n| F5 | **Integrity hash recomputation:** rev-001\'s `integrity_hash` is the literal token `sha256-rev1-master-data-classifiers-pinned` — **not a digest**. rev-002 must use a **real** `sha256` hex digest over the canonicalized JSON (sorted keys, no insignificant whitespace, UTF-8, no trailing newline), computed **after** all edits and **after** YAML↔JSON equivalence is confirmed. Field rename recommended: `integrity_hash` → `sha256:…` plus a sibling `hash_algorithm: "sha256"` and `hash_canonicalization: "json/sorted/utf8"` |\n| F6 | `history` append (do not rewrite rev-001\'s entry): `{ "revision_id": "rev-002", "change_type": ["ADD_CLASSIFIERS","MODIFY_CLASSIFIERS"], "classifiers_added": 2, "classifiers_modified": 4, "classifiers_removed": 0, "note": "CC newline separator + Luhn soft-fail; IBAN variable-length final group; ADDRESS newline boundary; MED-ID evidence retained" }` |\n| F7 | `pending_admin_review`: remains `[]` in the file; the change request itself is tracked **outside** the pinned artefact |\n| F8 | **Mirror paths that must be synced atomically and content-equivalent** (all three carry rev-001 today): `master_data_classifiers/ruleset.json`, `master_data_classifiers/ruleset.yaml`, `./ruleset.json` |\n| F9 | **Atomic sync procedure:** write each target to `*.tmp` → fsync → `os.replace()`; then verify (a) byte-equality of the two `.json` copies, (b) **semantic** deep-equality of `ruleset.yaml` vs `ruleset.json` (not byte equality), (c) recomputed sha256 == stored `integrity_hash` on **every** mirror. Any mismatch ⇒ abort and leave rev-001 in place |\n| F10 | **Detector re-pin sequence:** (1) quiesce detection workers; (2) drop compiled-regex/classifer caches; (3) load ruleset read-only, assert `len(classifiers) == 15`, assert `active_revision_id == "rev-002"`, assert middleware refuses writes; (4) run golden corpus §E3 → all assertions must pass; (5) compare §E1 deltas exactly; (6) on pass, flip `status` to PINNED and resume; on fail, execute §G rollback |\n\n---\n\n## (G) RISK & ROLLBACK\n\n| Change | False-positive risk | Precision/recall trade-off | Mitigation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **CC newline separator** | **Moderate.** `[ \\t\\-]*\\n?[ \\t\\-]*` can bridge `4-digit legit value` + newline + `4-digit legit value` (e.g. two consecutive dates/years in a table separated by newlines). Blank-line guard prevents paragraph bridging, but not adjacent-line bridging. | Recall **↑↑** (0→3 on `test_file.pdf`); precision **↓** because the generic `\\d{4}` branch now covers **any** 16-digit run, so the old issuer-prefix branch no longer discriminates. | Luhn tier + `currency/date proximity` negative heuristic; require ≥1 hyphen **or** uniform separator across all three separators (Admin decision D-1). **Note `4532-8910-4321-9081` fails Luhn** — Luhn alone cannot carry precision here. |\n| **CC Luhn soft-fail (0.86)** | Emits on Luhn-invalid 16-digit numbers — precisely the intended recall but the main FP vector. | Requires `validator_status: LUHN_FAIL` to be surfaced so downstream redaction reviewers see why. | Hard-gate alternative (Option 2) trades the entire fix away — **Admin decision D-2.** |\n| **IBAN variable final group** | **Low–moderate.** Optional `{1,3}` tail plus `\\n?` can extend a legitimate IBAN by a stray 1–3 char token on the next line; also `[A-Z0-9]` body with no checksum. | Recall **↑** (recovers `23`, enables `US39\\nOBAK`); precision **↓** slightly via over-extension. | Length post-filter 10–34 alnum; require ≥2 groups; optional ISO 13616 mod-97 check (would reject the current test IBAN — **verify before enabling**). |\n| **ADDRESS newline boundary** | **Low** (strictly reduces span size). **New small risk:** `[ \\t]`-only body may now **under**-extend addresses written with a newline between street and suite (`1200 Market\\nStreet Suite 400`) → under-redaction. | Recall **↓** marginally (under-extension cases), precision **↑↑** (no more label/SSN swallowing). | Add a specific `number\\nstreet-type` bridging case to the negative/positive corpus; consider a single `\\n?` allowed *inside* the street body only (Admin decision D-5). |\n| **MED-ID untouched (+ optional tightening)** | **None** if untouched; tightening to `\\d{6,12}` may **lose** existing true positives if the corpus contains alpha case refs. | Zero change recommended as default. | Do **not** tighten without a corpus scan (§B5). |\n| **New INSURANCE-MEMBER-ID** | **Low.** `[A-Z]{2}-\\d{9}-[A-Z]` is highly specific; residual risk is any unrelated `AB-123456789-X` style SKU/invoice code. | High precision, narrow recall. | Payer-prefix allowlist validator; disjointness with MED-ID. |\n| **New USERNAME** | **Low** *because* of mandatory label anchor; a naive un-anchored form was measured to match `administrator`, the email local-part, and a URL path segment — **rejected**. | Narrow recall (only labelled contexts); high precision. | Keep label anchor mandatory; `span_group: 1`; email/URL intersection assertions. Also note the **0.80 floor question** is moot (§C1) but Admin may codify a global floor. |\n\n**Rollback procedure to rev-001 (must be pre-staged before F1):**\n1. Keep an immutable, byte-identical snapshot of rev-001 (`ruleset.json`, `ruleset.yaml`, `./ruleset.json`) plus its recorded hash, taken **before** any F-step.\n2. Keep `rev-001` loadable by id (retain, don\'t delete, the revision object) so rollback = **re-pin**, not reconstruct: set `active_revision_id: rev-001`, `status: PINNED`, restore `ruleset_version: 1.0.0`, restore the original `integrity_hash` token/value.\n3. Atomic restore of all three mirror paths via `*.tmp` + `os.replace()`, in the reverse order of F9, then re-verify hash on each mirror.\n4. Purge compiled-pattern caches and re-load; re-run the **rev-001** golden baseline; assert the §E2 invariant spans are identical to the pre-change baseline.\n5. Record a `history` entry `{ "revision_id": "rev-002", "change_type": "ROLLBACK", "rolled_back_to": "rev-001", "reason": … }` — **append only, never rewrite rev-001\'s history**.\n6. Trigger condition: any §E3 assertion failure, any §E2 invariant violation, or any mirror hash mismatch. Rollback is manual (Human Admin) — **no auto-rollback on detection-quality metrics.**\n\n---\n\n## HUMAN ADMIN DECISION POINTS (blocking sign-off)\n- **D-1** CC: require ≥1 hyphen / uniform separators, or accept bare-newline bridging? (precision control)\n- **D-2** CC Luhn: **Option 1 soft-fail @0.86/threshold 0.85** (fixes the defect) vs **Option 2 hard gate @0.95** (leaves the defect unfixed, since the document card is Luhn-invalid).\n- **D-3** USERNAME: accept 0.86/0.85 context-anchored as specified, and/or codify a new global PII floor field.\n- **D-4** IBAN: remap `CLS-PII-IBAN-001` to `PII.FINANCIAL.IBAN`/`[IBAN]` (dormant enum activation) — yes/no.\n- **D-5** ADDRESS: allow a single internal `\\n?` between street number and street type to avoid under-extension — yes/no.\n- **D-6** MED-ID: leave pattern untouched (default) or adopt §B5 tightening.\n- **D-7** Corpus: supply distinct fingerprints for the two `New_Test_File.pdf` artefacts.\n\n**Nothing has been activated, pinned, or mutated. rev-001 remains the sole active revision.**\n\n```json\n{\n  "Name": "PII/PHI Span Detection agent",\n  "Inquiry": "DRAFT rev-002 CHANGE REQUEST SPECIFICATION (non-activating, for Human Admin approval) ... return the complete draft specification in a structured, copy-ready form suitable for Human Admin review and sign-off. Do not activate anything.",\n  "Mode": "Fulfill",\n  "Response": "Delivered full non-activating rev-002 draft spec covering (A)-(G) plus a new match_strategy block (H). Grounded on verbatim rev-001 definitions served read-only by master_classifier_repository_agent and on deterministic pattern execution in openai_code_interpreter. Key verified findings: CC separator class admits only one hyphen-or-space char so \'4532-\\\\n8910-4321-9081\' yields 0 matches (corrected pattern \'\\\\b(?:\\\\d{4}(?:[ \\\\t\\\\-]*\\\\n?[ \\\\t\\\\-]*)){3}\\\\d{4}\\\\b\' yields 3 matches); the document card 4532-8910-4321-9081 FAILS Luhn (digit-sum 72) so a hard Luhn gate would suppress the true positive - two-tier soft-fail proposed; IBAN rev-001 truncates at span end 33 leaving \' 23\' (corrected pattern recovers it to end 36, i.e. document [439,463]->[439,466]) and the \'US39\'+NEWLINE+\'OBAK\' fragment becomes detectable only with a bounded \'\\\\n?\' separator (space-only variant fails); ADDRESS rev-001 matched (0,55) swallowing \'\\\\nSocial Security Number\' because the trailing class contains \\\\s and digits, corrected pattern stops at (0,28) and shrinks document end 364->~341; MED-ID confirmed 0 matches for \'HI-902849102-B\' due to MC|MEM|PAT|REC anchoring; new INSURANCE-MEMBER-ID pattern \'\\\\b[A-Z]{2}-\\\\d{9}-[A-Z]\\\\b\' matches [403,417] as required and is disjoint from MED-ID by prefix alphabet; context-anchored USERNAME (capture-group, span_group 1) matches only \'mavance_admin\' ([83,96]) and rejects email local-parts, URL paths and \'administrator\', justifying 0.86 vs threshold 0.85. Flagged three premise corrections: rev-001 has NO global 0.85 PII floor (lowest is 0.80), NO validators field, NO match_strategy field, and NO per-match confidence field - all such elements are schema extensions. Provided schema paths (PII.IDENTIFIER.types += USERNAME; PHI.MEDICAL_IDENTIFIER.types += HEALTH_INSURANCE_MEMBER_ID; no new payment-card type needed), regression deltas and must-not-change span invariants, release/mirror plan (1.0.0->1.1.0, rev-002, three mirror paths, real sha256 canonicalized digest, atomic *.tmp+os.replace), detector re-pin sequence, risk table and manual rollback-to-rev-001 procedure, plus 7 blocking Human Admin decision points including the fact that the test corpus\'s own card is not Luhn-valid. No ruleset was mutated, pinned or activated; rev-001 remains the sole active revision."\n}\n```'}
