2026-10-19 12:40:44 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow: {"type": "AI", "text": "Here is the drafted **rev-002 Change Request** — non-activating, ready for your sign-off. It's built on verbatim rev-001 definitions and on the actual measured behaviour of the patterns against the three documents.\n\n⚠️ **First, three corrections I owe you from my earlier messages** — the detection agent verified these against the pinned source:\n\n1. **My \"0.85 PII confidence floor\" claim was wrong.** rev-001 has *no* global floor — only per-classifier `confidence_threshold` values. The lowest PII threshold is **0.80** (person name, NER), lowest PHI is **0.85** (condition). So no \"floor exception\" is technically needed for a username classifier. I stated otherwise; that was incorrect.\n2. **`4532-8910-4321-9081` — the actual card in `test_file.pdf` — FAILS the Luhn checksum** (digit-sum 72). This is critical: a hard Luhn gate would *suppress the very card we're trying to catch*. The draft proposes a soft-fail tier instead.\n3. **rev-001 has no `validators`, no `match_strategy`, and no per-match `confidence` field.** Every such element below is a *schema extension*, not a field edit.\n\n---\n\n# CHANGE REQUEST CR-002 — Ruleset `rev-001` → `rev-002`\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **Change request ID** | CR-002 |\n| **Target artifact** | `master_data_classifiers/ruleset.json` |\n| **From** | `rev-001` / version `1.0.0` / PINNED |\n| **To (proposed)** | `rev-002` / version `1.1.0` / PINNED |\n| **Change type** | `ADD_CLASSIFIERS` + `MODIFY_CLASSIFIERS` |\n| **Authorizer** | **Human Admin** (`ADMIN-ROOT-001`) — new approval token required |\n| **Status** | 🟡 **DRAFT — NOT ACTIVE. rev-001 remains the sole active revision.** |\n| **Classifiers** | 13 → **15** (2 added, 3 modified, 1 optional) |\n\n## 1. Why — measured defects\n\n| Defect | Evidence | Impact |\n|---|---|---|\n| **D1. Credit card blind to line breaks** | `4532-`↵`8910-4321-9081` ×3 in `test_file.pdf` → **0 matches**. Separator `[- ]?` admits one hyphen-or-space only. | 🔴 Payment card data survives unmasked |\n| **D2. IBAN truncation** | Matched `US39 OBAK 0123 4567 8901` `[439,463]`, dropped ` 23`. Fixed `{4}` grouping. Split `US39`↵`OBAK` fragment undetected. | 🟠 Partial identifier exposure |\n| **D3. Address over-extension** | `[293,364]` swallowed `\"\\nSocial Security Number\"`. Trailing class `[A-Za-z0-9\\s.,#]+` contains `\\s` **and** digits. | 🟡 Over-redaction + label corruption |\n| **D4. Insurance ID uncovered** | `HI-902849102-B` → 0 matches; anchor is `MC|MEM|PAT|REC` only. | 🟠 PHI identifier unmasked |\n| **D5. Username uncovered** | `mavance_admin` → no classifier exists. | 🟠 Credential unmasked |\n\n## 2. Schema extensions required\n\n| # | JSON path | Change |\n|---|---|---|\n| D-1 | `category_enums.PII.IDENTIFIER.types` | append `\"USERNAME\"` |\n| D-2 | `category_enums.PHI.MEDICAL_IDENTIFIER.types` | append `\"HEALTH_INSURANCE_MEMBER_ID\"` |\n| D-3 | `category_enums.PII.FINANCIAL.types` | **no change** — `CREDIT_CARD` and `IBAN` already exist |\n| D-4 | `classifiers[].validators` | **NEW field** (absent in rev-001) |\n| D-5 | `classifiers[].confidence` | **NEW field** (only `confidence_threshold` exists today) |\n| D-6 | `classifiers[].span_group` | **NEW field** (default 0; required 1 for username) |\n| D-7 | top-level `match_strategy` | **NEW field** (absent in rev-001) |\n\n> Note: `CLS-PII-IBAN-001` is currently bound to `PII.FINANCIAL.BANK_ACCOUNT`, leaving the enum member `PII.FINANCIAL.IBAN` **dormant/unused**. Optional normalization flagged as decision **D-4**.\n\n## 3. Modifications to existing classifiers\n\n### 3.1 `CLS-PII-CC-001` — credit card\n**Current:** `\\b(?:4\\d{3}|5[1-5]\\d{2}|6011|3[47]\\d{2})[- ]?\\d{4}[- ]?\\d{4}[- ]?\\d{4}\\b|\\b\\d{4}-\\d{4}-\\d{4}-\\d{4}\\b`\n\n**Proposed:**\n```json\n\"pattern\": \"\\\\b(?:\\\\d{4}(?:[ \\\\t\\\\-]*\\\\n?[ \\\\t\\\\-]*)){3}\\\\d{4}\\\\b\",\n\"validators\": [\n  { \"id\": \"luhn_mod10\", \"type\": \"checksum\", \"algorithm\": \"LUHN\",\n    \"on_pass\": { \"confidence\": 0.99, \"status\": \"LUHN_PASS\" },\n    \"on_fail\": { \"confidence\": 0.86, \"status\": \"LUHN_FAIL\", \"emit_metadata\": true } }\n],\n\"confidence_threshold\": 0.85\n```\nAccepts hyphen/space runs + **at most one newline** per separator; **blank lines still rejected** (prevents paragraph bridging).\n\n> 🔴 **Luhn conflict:** `4532-8910-4321-9081` → **FAIL** (digit-sum 72). A hard gate suppresses the true positive. Hence soft-fail at 0.86 with `LUHN_FAIL` surfaced for reviewer attention. **Blocking decision D-2.**\n\n### 3.2 `CLS-PII-IBAN-001` — bank account\n**Current:** `\\b[A-Z]{2}\\d{2}(?:\\s?[A-Z0-9]{4}){3,7}\\b`\n\n**Proposed:**\n```json\n\"pattern\": \"\\\\b[A-Z]{2}\\\\d{2}(?:[ \\\\t]*\\\\n?[ \\\\t]*[A-Z0-9]{4}){1,7}(?:[ \\\\t]*\\\\n?[ \\\\t]*[A-Z0-9]{1,3})?\\\\b\",\n\"validators\": [ { \"id\": \"alnum_length\", \"type\": \"post_filter\", \"spec\": \"cleaned alnum length in 10..34\" } ]\n```\nAdds variable-length final group → recovers ` 23`, span becomes `[439,466]`. The split `US39`↵`OBAK` fragment becomes detectable **only** because of the bounded `\\n?` — do not narrow to space-only.\n\n### 3.3 `CLS-PII-ADDRESS-001` — street address\n**Current:** `\\b\\d{1,5}\\s+[A-Za-z0-9\\s.,]+(?:…Way|Lane|Drive…)(?:[A-Za-z0-9\\s.,#]+)?(?:,\\s+…,\\s+[A-Z]{2}\\s+\\d{5})?\\b`\n\n**Proposed:**\n```json\n\"pattern\": \"\\\\b\\\\d{1,5}[ \\\\t]+(?:[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9.\\\\-#]*[ \\\\t]+){0,6}(?:Terrace|Street|St|Avenue|Ave|Road|Rd|Boulevard|Blvd|Way|Lane|Ln|Drive|Dr)\\\\b(?:[ \\\\t]*,[ \\\\t]*(?:Suite|Ste|Unit|Apt|Bldg|Floor|Fl)[ \\\\t]*#?[0-9A-Za-z-]+|[ \\\\t]+(?:Suite|Ste|Unit|Apt|Bldg|Floor|Fl)[ \\\\t]*#?[0-9A-Za-z-]+)?(?:,[ \\\\t]+[A-Za-z .]+,[ \\\\t]+[A-Z]{2}[ \\\\t]+\\\\d{5}(?:-\\\\d{4})?)?\",\n\"validators\": [ { \"id\": \"truncate_at_newline\", \"type\": \"post_filter\", \"spec\": \"trim at last [ \\\\t] token before any \\\\n\" } ]\n```\nBody uses **`[ \\t]` only, never `\\s`** → cannot enter a newline+label boundary. Verified: over-extended `(0,55)` → correctly `(0,28)`. Document end shifts `364 → ≈341` (matches the narrowing you already applied manually).\n\n### 3.4 `CLS-PHI-MED-ID-001` — medical case ref\n**Recommended: leave untouched.** Confirmed 0 matches for `HI-…`; correct fix is a *separate* classifier, not widening this anchor (a case ref ≠ insurance member ID). Optional tightening `\\b(?:MC|MEM|PAT|REC)-\\d{6,12}(?:-[A-Z0-9]{1,2})?\\b` flagged as decision **D-6** — only after a corpus scan, since it may drop alpha case refs.\n\n## 4. New classifiers\n\n### 4.1 `CLS-PII-USERNAME-001`\n```json\n{\n  \"classifier_id\": \"CLS-PII-USERNAME-001\",\n  \"category\": \"PII.IDENTIFIER.USERNAME\",\n  \"pattern\": \"(?:\\\\b(?:Account Name|Username|Account|Login|User)[ \\\\t]*:[ \\\\t]*)([a-z][a-z0-9._\\\\-]{2,31})(?![A-Za-z0-9.@\\\\-])\",\n  \"span_group\": 1,\n  \"confidence\": 0.86,\n  \"confidence_threshold\": 0.85,\n  \"priority\": 3,\n  \"mask_token\": \"[USERNAME]\",\n  \"validators\": [\n    { \"id\": \"label_anchor_required\", \"type\": \"context_anchor\", \"spec\": \"label + colon mandatory\" },\n    { \"id\": \"not_email_localpart\", \"type\": \"negative_lookahead_guard\", \"spec\": \"reject if adjacent to @ or URL token\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n**Measured:** matches **only** `mavance_admin` `[83,96]` in the real document. Against a probe containing `marcus.vance@example.com`, `https://portal.example.com/mavance_admin`, and `administrator` → **only the username matched**. The mandatory label anchor is what justifies **0.86 ≥ 0.85**; a naive un-anchored form measured ~0.75 *and* over-matched, so **no 0.75 variant is proposed.**\n\n> Implementation note: `(?<=…)` fails — `(?:Account|Username|User)` is variable-width. The consuming-prefix + `span_group: 1` form is **mandatory**.\n\n### 4.2 `CLS-PHI-INSURANCE-MEMBER-ID-001`\n```json\n{\n  \"classifier_id\": \"CLS-PHI-INSURANCE-MEMBER-ID-001\",\n  \"category\": \"PHI.MEDICAL_IDENTIFIER.HEALTH_INSURANCE_MEMBER_ID\",\n  \"pattern\": \"\\\\b[A-Z]{2}-\\\\d{9}-[A-Z]\\\\b\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.93,\n  \"confidence_threshold\": 0.90,\n  \"priority\": 2,\n  \"mask_token\": \"[INSURANCE_MEMBER_ID]\",\n  \"validators\": [\n    { \"id\": \"issuer_prefix_allowlist\", \"type\": \"dictionary_and_heuristic\", \"spec\": \"2-char payer prefix (HI, BC, AH, UN, …) — Admin to confirm closed list\" },\n    { \"id\": \"segment_shape\", \"type\": \"heuristic\", \"spec\": \"9 digits + 1 alpha check\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n**Measured:** `HI-902849102-B` → `[403,417]`, length 14. ✅\nPrefix alphabets are **disjoint** from MED-ID (`HI` vs `MC|MEM|PAT|REC`), so the two cannot overlap by construction — but this must be **asserted by test**, not assumed.\n\n## 5. `match_strategy` block (new — rev-001 has none)\n```json\n\"match_strategy\": {\n  \"overlap_resolution\": \"deterministic\",\n  \"order\": [\"start_offset:asc\", \"match_length:desc\", \"priority:asc\", \"confidence:desc\", \"classifier_id:asc\"],\n  \"on_tie\": \"keep_first\",\n  \"dedupe\": \"identical_start_end_category\",\n  \"span_source\": \"span_group_if_defined_else_full_match\"\n}\n```\n\n## 6. Regression plan — expected deltas\n\n| Document | Classifier | rev-001 | rev-002 | Δ |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| test_file.pdf | CREDIT_CARD | **0** | **3** | **+3** |\n| test_file.pdf | IBAN | 1 @ `[439,463]` | 1 @ `[439,466]` | end **+3** |\n| test_file.pdf | ADDRESS | end 364 | end ≈341 | end **−23** |\n| test_file.pdf | INSURANCE_MEMBER_ID | — | 1 @ `[403,417]` | **+1** |\n| Marcus Vance …Record.pdf | USERNAME | — | 1 @ `[83,96]` | **+1** |\n| New_Test_File.pdf (both) | all | baseline | baseline | **0 expected — must be measured** |\n\n**Must NOT change (byte-identical assertions):** person name, email, phone, passport, IP, SSN, DOB, DL, condition spans and offsets; the 9 untouched classifiers' `priority`/`threshold`. Plus: `Σ USERNAME ∩ Σ EMAIL = ∅`, `Σ INS ∩ Σ MED-ID = ∅`, and the address end must sit **before** the SSN start.\n\n**Negative corpus:** `administrator`, `The US39 code`, `AB12`, `1234↵5678↵9012`, `4532-↵↵8910-4321-9081`, `Account mavance_admin` (no colon) → **zero matches**.\n\n> ⚠️ Corpus ambiguity: `New_Test_File.pdf` appears twice in our history. I need **distinct fingerprints (sha256 or mtime)** per artifact or the delta table can't be bound to a specific file. — **D-7**\n\n## 7. Release & mirror plan\n\n| Step | Action |\n|---|---|\n| F1–F2 | `ruleset_version: 1.0.0 → 1.1.0`; `metadata.revision: 1 → 2`; `active_revision_id: rev-001 → rev-002` |\n| F3–F4 | `status: PINNED` **only after token**; new `approval_actor` / `approval_token` / `approval_timestamp` — must **not** reuse rev-001's token |\n| F5 | 🔧 **Real** sha256: rev-001's `integrity_hash` is the literal string `sha256-rev1-master-data-classifiers-pinned` — **not a digest**. rev-002 should carry a genuine sha256 hex over canonicalized JSON (sorted keys, UTF-8, no trailing newline), plus `hash_algorithm` / `hash_canonicalization` siblings |\n| F6 | Append history entry: `ADD_CLASSIFIERS + MODIFY_CLASSIFIERS`, added 2, modified 4, removed 0. **Never rewrite rev-001's entry** |\n| F8 | Three mirrors synced atomically & content-equivalent: `master_data_classifiers/ruleset.json`, `master_data_classifiers/ruleset.yaml`, `./ruleset.json` |\n| F9 | `*.tmp` → fsync → `os.replace()`; verify JSON byte-equality, YAML**semantic** equality, and hash on every mirror. Any mismatch ⇒ **abort, rev-001 stays** |\n| F10 | Detector re-pin: quiesce → drop compiled caches → load read-only → assert `len(classifiers)==15` and `active_revision_id==\"rev-002\"` and writes refused → run golden corpus → flip to PINNED. On fail ⇒ rollback |\n\n## 8. Risk summary\n\n| Change | FP risk | Mitigation |\n|---|---|---|\n| CC newline separator | **Moderate** — can bridge adjacent 4-digit values across lines | Soft-fail Luhn tier; optional uniform-separator requirement (D-1) |\n| CC Luhn soft-fail | Emits Luhn-invalid 16-digit runs — the main FP vector | Surface `LUHN_FAIL` to reviewer |\n| IBAN variable final group | Low–moderate — optional tail may over-extend | Alnum-length 10–34 post-filter |\n| ADDRESS newline boundary | **Low**; small *new* under-extension risk for `street`↵`Suite` | Add bridging case to corpus (D-5) |\n| USERNAME | Low (label anchor mandatory) | Email/URL intersection assertions |\n| INSURANCE_MEMBER_ID | Low (highly specific shape) | Payer prefix allowlist |\n\n**Rollback:** keep a byte-identical rev-001 snapshot *before* F1; retain rev-001 loadable by id so rollback is a **re-pin, not a reconstruction**; atomic restore of all three mirrors; re-run the rev-001 baseline asserting §6 invariants; append a `ROLLBACK` history entry. Manual, Human-Admin-triggered — no auto-rollback.\n\n---\n\n## 🔴 Blocking decision points — your sign-off needed\n\n| # | Decision | Recommended |\n|---|---|---|\n| **D-1** | CC separators: require ≥1 hyphen / uniform separators, or accept bare-newline bridging? | accept newline, require uniform |\n| **D-2** | **CC Luhn: Option 1 soft-fail @0.86/thr 0.85 (fixes the defect) vs Option 2 hard gate @0.95 (defect stays unfixed — card is Luhn-invalid)** | **Option 1** |\n| **D-3** | Username at 0.86/thr 0.85 context-anchored as specified — and do you also want a *global PII floor* codified as a new field? | accept 0.86; no global floor |\n| **D-4** | Remap `CLS-PII-IBAN-001` → `PII.FINANCIAL.IBAN` / `[IBAN]` (activates dormant enum)? | yes |\n| **D-5** | Address: allow a single internal `\\n?` between number and street type to avoid under-extension? | no (keep strict) |\n| **D-6** | MED-ID: leave untouched (default) or adopt tightening? | leave untouched |\n| **D-7** | Supply distinct fingerprints for the two `New_Test_File.pdf` artifacts | required before regression |\n\nOnce you answer D-1 … D-7 and issue the **rev-002 approval token**, the revision can be authored, tested against the golden corpus, mirror-synced, and detectors re-pinned. Until then **rev-001 remains the sole active revision** and nothing here has been activated."}
