ange.\\n\\nCANDIDATE PATTERNS (human-readable; report your executed form):\\n1. CLS-PII-CC-001 (MODIFIED): \\\\b(?:\\\\d{4}(?:[ \\\\t\\\\-]*\\\\n?[ \\\\t\\\\-]*)){3}\\\\d{4}\\\\b  + NEW uniform-separator validator (reject match if the three separators are not all-same-class) + Luhn soft-fail as in D-2.\\n2. CLS-PII-IBAN-001 (MODIFIED): \\\\b[A-Z]{2}\\\\d{2}(?:[ \\\\t]*\\\\n?[ \\\\t]*[A-Z0-9]{4}){1,7}(?:[ \\\\t]*\\\\n?[ \\\\t]*[A-Z0-9]{1,3})?\\\\b + alnum-length 10..34 post-filter + D-4 category/mask remap.\\n3. CLS-PII-ADDRESS-001 (MODIFIED): \\\\b\\\\d{1,5}[ \\\\t]+(?:[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9.\\\\-#]*[ \\\\t]+){0,6}(?:Terrace|Street|St|Avenue|Ave|Road|Rd|Boulevard|Blvd|Way|Lane|Ln|Drive|Dr)\\\\b(?:[ \\\\t]*,[ \\\\t]*(?:Suite|Ste|Unit|Apt|Bldg|Floor|Fl)[ \\\\t]*#?[0-9A-Za-z-]+|[ \\\\t]+(?:Suite|Ste|Unit|Apt|Bldg|Floor|Fl)[ \\\\t]*#?[0-9A-Za-z-]+)?(?:,[ \\\\t]+[A-Za-z .]+,[ \\\\t]+[A-Z]{2}[ \\\\t]+\\\\d{5}(?:-\\\\d{4})?)?  + truncate_at_newline post-filter.\\n4. CLS-PHI-MED-ID-001: UNCHANGED (confirm 0 matches still).\\n5. CLS-PII-USERNAME-001 (NEW): (?:\\\\b(?:Account Name|Username|Account|Login|User)[ \\\\t]*:[ \\\\t]*)([a-z][a-z0-9._\\\\-]{2,31})(?![A-Za-z0-9.@\\\\-]) with span_group 1, confidence 0.86, threshold 0.85.\\n6. CLS-PHI-INSURANCE-MEMBER-ID-001 (NEW): \\\\b[A-Z]{2}-\\\\d{9}-[A-Z]\\\\b, confidence 0.93, threshold 0.90.\\n\\nREQUIRED OUTPUT \\u2014 for each item give measured values, not assertions:\\n(A) test_file.pdf: exact count + start/end offsets + matched_text for CC (expect 3), IBAN (expect 1 at [439,466] with text ending \\"23\\"), ADDRESS (expect 1, end ~341, confirm NO \\"\\\\n\\" in span and end < SSN start 366), INSURANCE_MEMBER_ID (expect 1 at [403,417]).\\n(B) Marcus Vance System Account Record.pdf: USERNAME (expect 1 at [83,96], text \\"mavance_admin\\"); confirm all other spans unchanged.\\n(C) Uniform-separator validator behaviour: does test_file.pdf\'s card 4532-<newline>8910-4321-9081 PASS or FAIL the uniform-separator check? Be explicit \\u2014 this determines whether the D-1 constraint would suppress the very matches we want. Report the separator class detected for each of the three occurrences. Also test: \\"4532 8910 4321 9081\\" (uniform spaces -> pass), \\"4532-8910 4321-9081\\" (mixed -> reject), \\"4532-\\\\n8910-4321-9081\\" (mixed hyphen/newline -> ?), and \\"4111 1111 1111 1111\\" (uniform space, Luhn pass -> 0.99).\\n(D) Luhn results with actual digit-sums: 4111111111111111, 4012888888881881, 4532891043219081.\\n(E) \\u00a7E3 assertions 1-8: PASS/FAIL each. Confirm \\u03a3 INS \\u2229 \\u03a3 MED-ID = \\u2205 and \\u03a3 USERNAME \\u2229 \\u03a3 EMAIL = \\u2205.\\n(F) Negative corpus: administrator, \\"The US39 code\\", AB12, \\"1234\\\\n5678\\\\n9012\\", \\"4532-\\\\n\\\\n8910-4321-9081\\", \\"Account mavance_admin\\" (no colon) -> each must yield 0 matches.\\n(G) New_Test_File.pdf delta rows: mark BLOCKED (unbound \\u2014 fingerprints outstanding per D-7). Do not report a number.\\n(H) Any NEW false positives or span-behaviour changes the decisions introduced vs the prior draft \\u2014 especially anything caused by D-1 uniform separators or D-4 unmasking the IBAN category remap.\\n(I) Confirm explicitly that rev-001 was not mutated and that this was a shadow evaluation only.", "mode": "Fulfill"}}'}
