2026-10-19 12:45:28 BST | INFO     | NeuroSan:_log:821 - NeuroSan - {"message": "Result from OpenAI Tool: [{'type': 'server_tool_call', 'name': 'code_interpreter', 'id': 'ci_07e63e632c7363a2006ad602cc424887d2a354ec5435f583eb', 'args': {'code': "import re\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Dict, Union\n\ndef classify_separator(separator: str) -> str:\n    if '\\n' in separator:\n        return 'NEWLINE_BEARING'\n    elif '-' in separator and all(c == '-' or c.isspace() for c in separator):\n        return 'HYPHEN'\n    elif separator.strip() == '':\n        return 'SPACE_RUN'\n    else:\n        return 'OTHER'\n\ndef is_uniformly_accepted(classes: List[str]) -> bool:\n    return len(set(classes)) == 1 and classes[0] in {'HYPHEN', 'SPACE_RUN', 'NEWLINE_BEARING'}\n\ndef process_cc_tests(test_strings: List[str]) -> List[Dict[str, Union[str, List[str], bool]]]:\n    results = []\n    cc_regex = re.compile(r'(\\d{4})(.*?)(\\d{4})(.*?)(\\d{4})(.*?)(\\d{4})')\n\n    for test_string in test_strings:\n        match = cc_regex.match(test_string)\n        if match:\n            separators = match.groups()[1::2]  # Get the three separators\n            classes = [classify_separator(sep) for sep in separators]\n            uniformly_accepted = is_uniformly_accepted(classes)\n            results.append({\n                'test_string': test_string,\n                'separators': separators,\n                'classes': classes,\n                'uniformly_accepted': uniformly_accepted\n            })\n    return results\n\ndef test_negative_corpus(negative_corpus: List[str]) -> List[Dict[str, Union[str, List[Tuple[int, int, str]]]]]:\n    results = []\n    cc_negative_results = []\n    regex_patterns = {\n        'CC': r'\\b\\d{4}([^\\n]*?)\\d{4}([^\\n]*?)\\d{4}([^\\n]*?)\\d{4}\\b',\n        'IBAN': r'\\b\\w{10,34}\\b',\n        'ADDRESS': r'\\b[\\w\\s,]+(?:\\n|$)',\n        'USERNAME': r'\\b[a-zA-Z0-9._-]{3,30}\\b', # Simple pattern for demonstration\n        'INSURANCE': r'\\b\\d{5,10}\\b' # Simple pattern for demonstration\n    }\n\n    for string in negative_corpus:\n        matches = {name: [] for name in regex_patterns}\n        \n        for name, pattern in regex_patterns.items():\n            for match in re.finditer(pattern, string):\n                matches[name].append((match.start(), match.end(), match.group()))\n        \n        results.append({\n            'string': string,\n            'matches': matches\n        })\n        \n        # Specifically checking for CC matching with separator validation\n        cc_match = re.match(regex_patterns['CC'], string)\n        \n        if cc_match:\n            separators = cc_match.groups()\n            classes = [classify_separator(sep) for sep in separators]\n            uniformly_accepted = is_uniformly_accepted(classes)\n            cc_negative_results.append({\n                'string': string,\n                'separators': separators,\n                'classes': classes,\n                'uniformly_accepted': uniformly_accepted\n            })\n    \n    return results, cc_negative_results\n\n# Define the test data\ncc_test_strings = [\n    '4532-\\n8910-4321-9081',\n    '4532 8910 4321 9081',\n    '4532-8910 4321-9081',\n    '4532-\\n8910-4321-9081',\n    '4111 1111 1111 1111'\n]\n\nnegative_corpus = [\n    'administrator',\n    'The US39 code',\n    'AB12',\n    '1234\\n5678\\n9012',\n    '4532-\\n\\n8910-4321-9081',\n    'Account mavance_admin'\n]\n\n# Process the tests\ncc_results = process_cc_tests(cc_test_strings)\nnegative_results, cc_negative_results = test_negative_corpus(negative_corpus)\n\n(cc_results, cc_negative_results, negative_results)"}, 'extras': {'container_id': 'cntr_6ad602cbd42081918da7438717a0579804244d9dbd07997c'}}, {'type': 'server_tool_result', 'tool_call_id': 'ci_07e63e632c7363a2006ad602cc424887d2a354ec5435f583eb', 'status': 'success'}, {'type': 'text', 'text': "Here are the results for the tests and negative corpus strings:\n\n### CC Test Strings\n\n1.