lassifier\n\nThe label alternation `(?:Account Name|Username|Account|Login|User)` binds the bare word **\"User\"** in `User Role: Senior Systems Administrator` and captures **`Role`** as a username. This fires on **both** documents — it would emit a spurious redaction span in every file containing that label.\n\nFix: drop bare `User` from the label set and add `(?!\\s*Role\\b)` as a guard. Label set becomes `Account Name|Username|User Name|Login|Account`, colon mandatory immediately after the full label.\n\n→ **New decision D-9: approve the tightened label set?** (recommend yes — non-negotiable, this is a false positive)\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ Correction I owe you\n\nI said the Marcus Vance record's username sat at `[83,96]`. **That's wrong** — `[83,96]` is `test_file.pdf`'s offset. Verified positions:\n\n| Document | `mavance_admin` |\n|---|---|\n| test_file.pdf | **[83, 96]** (13 chars) |\n| Marcus Vance System Account Record.pdf | **[56, 69]** (13 chars) |\n\nAny redaction already performed used the correct text, so no artifact is affected — but the spec figure needs correcting, and that's now done.\n\n---\n\n## 📊 Measured shadow results (before → after)\n\n### `test_file.pdf` (784 chars confirmed; a single ambiguous terminal LF would make it 785 — all offsets identical either way)\n\n| Classifier | rev-001 measured | Candidate (Variant A) | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| CREDIT_CARD | **0** | **3** @ `[561,581]` `[694,714]` `[764,784]` | ✅ fixed |\n| IBAN | 1 @ `[439,463]` — endswith \"23\" = **FALSE** | 1 @ `[439,466]` — endswith \"23\" = **TRUE** | ✅ fixed |\n| ADDRESS | 1 @ `[293,364]` — **contains `\\n` + \"Social Security Number\"** | 1 @ `[293,341]` — clean, end 341 < SSN 366 | ✅ fixed |\n| INSURANCE_MEMBER_ID | *absent* | `HI-902849102-B` @ `[403,417]` | ✅ new |\n| MED-ID | 0 | 0 | ✅ unchanged |\n| `US39`↵`OBAK` fragment | 0 | **still 0** @ `[634,644)` | ⚠️ see note |\n\n**Luhn:** all three cards fail (digit-sum 72). Under locked **Option 1** that means confiden