 | Prio | Mask |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| CLS-PII-SSN-001 | SSN / National ID | regex | `\\b\\d{3}-\\d{2}-\\d{4}\\b` | 0.95 | 1 | partial (last 4 preserved) |\n| CLS-PII-CC-001 | Credit Card | regex + `luhn_soft_fail` | `\\b(?:(?:4\\d{3}|5[1-5]\\d{2}|6011|3[47]\\d{2}|\\d{4})(?:(?:-(?:\\n|\\r\\n)?\\d{4}-(?:(?:\\n|\\r\\n)?\\d{4})-(?:\\n|\\r\\n)?\\d{4})|(?:\\s\\d{4}\\s\\d{4}\\s\\d{4})))\\b` — D-8 Variant A line-wrap normalization; Luhn pass 0.99 / fail 0.86, threshold 0.85 | 0.85 | 1 | partial (PCI last-4) |\n| CLS-PII-EMAIL-001 | Email Address | regex | `\\b[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\\.[A-Za-z]{2,}\\b` | 0.95 | 2 | partial (local part) |\n| CLS-PII-PHONE-001 | Telephone Number | regex | `(?:\\+?1[-. ]?)?(?:\\(\\d{3}\\)\\|\\b\\d{3})[-. ]?\\d{3}[-. ]?\\d{4}\\b` | 0.90 | 2 | partial (keep +1) |\n| CLS-PII-IP-001 | IP Address (v4 & v6) | regex | `\\b(?:(?:25[0-5]\\|2[0-4][0-9]\\|[01]?[0-9][0-9]?)\\.){3}(?:25[0-5]\\|2[0-4][0-9]\\|[01]?[0-9][0-9]?)\\b\\|\\b(?:[0-9a-fA-F]{1,4}:){7}[0-9a-fA-F]{1,4}\\b` | 0.90 | 3 | full |\n| CLS-PII-DOB-001 | Date of Birth | regex | `\\b(?:19\\|20)\\d{2}-(?:0[1-9]\\|1[0-2])-(?:0[1-9]\\|[12]\\d\\|3[01])\\b\\|\\b(?:January\\|…\\|December)\\s+(?:0?[1-9]\\|[12]\\d\\|3[01]),\\s+(?:19\\|20)\\d{2}\\b` | 0.85 | 3 | full |\n| CLS-PII-IBAN-001 | Bank Account (IBAN) | regex | `\\b[A-Z]{2}\\d{2}(?:\\s?[A-Z0-9]{4}){3,7}(?:\\s?[A-Z0-9]{1,4})?\\b` (variable-length final group) | 0.90 | 2 | partial (keep country+check, last 2–4) |\n| CLS-PII-PASSPORT-001 | Passport Number | regex | `\\b[A-Z]\\d{8,9}\\b` | 0.85 | 3 | full |\n| CLS-PII-DL-001 | Driver\'s License | regex | `\\bDL-[A-Z0-9]{6,12}(?:-[A-Z]{2})?\\b` | 0.85 | 3 | full |\n| CLS-PII-ADDRESS-001 | Street Address | regex | `\\b\\d{1,5}[ \\t]+[A-Za-z0-9., \\t]+(?:Terrace\\|Street\\|St\\|Avenue\\|Ave\\|Road\\|Rd\\|Boulevard\\|Blvd\\|Way\\|Lane\\|Ln\\|Drive\\|Dr)(?:,?[ \\t]+(?:Suite\\|Ste\\|Apt\\|Unit\\|#)[ \\t]+[A-Za-z0-9-]+)?,[ \\t]+[A-Za-z \\t]+,[ \\t]+[A-Z]{2}[ \\t]+\\d{5}(?:-\\d{4})?\\b` (full form) **or** same without `, City, ST ZIP` tail — horizontal-whitespace bounded to prevent newline over-match | 0.85 | 4 | partial (keep city/state/zip) |\n| CLS-PII-NAME-001 | Full Name | **ner** | `entity_types: ["PERSON"]` | 0.80 | 5 | full |\n| CLS-PHI-MED-ID-001 | Medical Case Ref / Patient Member ID | regex | `\\b(?:MC\\|MEM\\|PAT\\|REC)-[A-Za-z0-9-]{4,15}\\b` | 0.90 | 2 | full |\n| CLS-PHI-CONDITION-001 | Health Condition / Prescription / Allergy | **dictionary_and_heuristic** | terms: `penicillin allergy`, `allergy`, `Hypertension`, `hypertension`, `prescription adjustment`, `emergency dispensation`, `medical dispensation` | 0.85 | 3 | full |\n| CLS-PII-USERNAME-001 | System Account Username | **regex_context** | `(?i:\\b(?:Account Name\\|Username\\|User Name\\|Login\\|Account):[ \\t]*)(?!Role\\b)([a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9._-]{2,30})\\b` — D-9 negative lookahead guard; base confidence 0.86 | 0.85 | 3 | full |\n| CLS-PHI-INSURANCE-MEMBER-ID-001 | Health Insurance Member ID / Policy No. | regex | `\\b(?:HI\\|INS\\|POL\\|GRP)-[A-Za-z0-9-]{6,16}\\b\\|(?i:\\bHealth Insurance (?:Number\\|ID\\|Member ID):[ \\t]*)([A-Za-z0-9-]+)\\b` — base confidence 0.90 | 0.85 | 2 | partial (keep plan prefix) |\n\n**Special rule types present:** `regex` (12), `ner` (1: PERSON via CLS-PII-NAME-001), `dictionary_and_heuristic` (1), `regex_context` (1). **Validator:** `luhn_soft_fail` on CLS-PII-CC-001 only. **Heuristics:** label-context anchoring with negative lookahead (username, insurance member ID), whitespace-scoped bounding (address).\n\n### 3. Notes for citing / consuming this revision\n- Cite as: **`rev-002` / ruleset_version `1.1.0` / integrity_hash `sha256-rev2-master-data-classifiers-pinned`**, approved by `ADMIN-ROOT-001` on `2026-10-19T13:10:00Z`.\n- Full verbatim JSON body (all 15 classifier objects, taxonomy, and history) was read from `master_data_classifiers/ruleset.json` (340 lines) in this session; the table above is a faithful condensation and the file remains the governing text.\n- Two items worth a caller\'s attention, surfaced without altering state (reads are read-only; I do not edit the ruleset):\n  1. **Taxonomy types without a dedicated classifier** in this revision: `NATIONAL_ID`, `BANK_ACCOUNT`, `CVV`, `PATIENT_ID`, `MEDICAL_CASE_REF`, `ALLERGY`, `CONDITION`, `PRESCRIPTION`, `CLINICAL_NOTE`. These are category declarations only and are covered (if at all) indirectly — e.g. CVV has no pattern, and ALLERGY/CONDITION/PRESCRIPTION/CLINICAL_NOTE fall under the single `CLS-PHI-CONDITION-001` dictionary.\n  2. **YAML mirror artifact:** in `ruleset.yaml` the `CLS-PII-ADDRESS-001` pattern is emitted with literal line continuations inside `[ \\t]` character classes, which would change the pattern if a consumer parsed the YAML raw. Use the JSON as authoritative.\n\n```json\n{\n  "Name": "master_data_classifiers_ruleset_registry",\n  "Inquiry": "Provide the active pinned ruleset (rev-002, version 1.1.0) including PII/PHI categories, regex patterns, NER types, dictionary terms, heuristics, and confidence thresholds.",\n  "Mode": "Fulfill",\n  "Response": "Served from master_data_classifiers/ruleset.json (read-only). Active revision: rev-002, ruleset_version 1.1.0, status PINNED, approved by Human Admin (ADMIN-ROOT-001) at 2026-10-19T13:10:00Z, approval_token AUTH-TOKEN-ADMIN-REV2-APPROVED-20261019-ROOT, integrity_hash sha256-rev2-master-data-classifiers-pinned. pending_admin_review: []. 15 classifiers. Categories: PII{PERSON_NAME; IDENTIFIER(SSN,NATIONAL_ID,PASSPORT,DRIVERS_LICENSE,USERNAME); CONTACT(EMAIL,PHONE_NUMBER); LOCATION(STREET_ADDRESS,IP_ADDRESS); FINANCIAL(CREDIT_CARD,BANK_ACCOUNT,IBAN,CVV); DEMOGRAPHIC(DATE_OF_BIRTH)} and PHI{MEDICAL_IDENTIFIER(PATIENT_ID,MEDICAL_CASE_REF,HEALTH_INSURANCE_MEMBER_ID); HEALTH_DATA(ALLERGY,CONDITION,PRESCRIPTION,CLINICAL_NOTE)}. Classifiers: CLS-PII-SSN-001 regex \\\\b\\\\d{3}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{4}\\\\b th=0.95; CLS-PII-CC-001 regex with line-wrap normalization + validator luhn_soft_fail (luhn_pass_confidence 0.99, luhn_fail_confidence 0.86, threshold 0.85) th=0.85; CLS-PII-EMAIL-001 regex \\\\b[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\\\\.[A-Za-z]{2,}\\\\b th=0.95; CLS-PII-PHONE-001 regex NA phone format th=0.90; CLS-PII-IP-001 regex IPv4/IPv6 th=0.90 (full mask); CLS-PII-DOB-001 regex ISO-8601 + month-name th=0.85 (full mask); CLS-PII-IBAN-001 regex \\\\b[A-Z]{2}\\\\d{2}(?:\\\\s?[A-Z0-9]{4}){3,7}(?:\\\\s?[A-Z0-9]{1,4})?\\\\b th=0.90 (partial); CLS-PII-PASSPORT-001 regex \\\\b[A-Z]\\\\d{8,9}\\\\b th=0.85; CLS-PII-DL-001 regex \\\\bDL-[A-Z0-9]{6,12}(?:-[A-Z]{2})?\\\\b th=0.85; CLS-PII-ADDRESS-001 regex street address bounded by horizontal whitespace [ \\\\t] only th=0.85 (partial, keeps city/state/zip); CLS-PII-NAME-001 type=ner entity_types=[PERSON] th=0.80; CLS-PHI-MED-ID-001 regex \\\\b(?:MC|MEM|PAT|REC)-[A-Za-z0-9-]{4,15}\\\\b th=0.90; CLS-PHI-CONDITION-001 type=dictionary_and_heuristic terms=[penicillin allergy, allergy, Hypertension, hypertension, prescription adjustment, emergency dispensation, medical dispensation] th=0.85; CLS-PII-USERNAME-001 type=regex_context with label anchor (Account Name|Username|User Name|Login|Account) plus (?!Role\\\\b) guard (D-9), base confidence 0.86, th=0.85; CLS-PHI-INSURANCE-MEMBER-ID-001 regex \\\\b(?:HI|INS|POL|GRP)-[A-Za-z0-9-]{6,16}\\\\b|(?i:\\\\bHealth Insurance (?:Number|ID|Member ID):[ \\\\t]*)([A-Za-z0-9-]+)\\\\b, base confidence 0.90, th=0.85 (partial, keeps plan prefix). Heuristics in ruleset: label-context anchoring with negative lookahead, whitespace-scoped bounding, Luhn soft-fail. History: rev-001/1.0.0 INIT (13 classifiers); rev-002/1.1.0 UPDATE (+CLS-PII-USERNAME-001, +CLS-PHI-INSURANCE-MEMBER-ID-001; modified CLS-PII-CC-001, CLS-PII-IBAN-001, CLS-PII-ADDRESS-001) per D-8 Variant A and D-9. Caveats (no state change made): declared types NATIONAL_ID, BANK_ACCOUNT, CVV, PATIENT_ID, MEDICAL_CASE_REF, ALLERGY, CONDITION, PRESCRIPTION, CLINICAL_NOTE have no dedicated classifier in this revision; the ruleset.yaml mirror\'s CLS-PII-ADDRESS-001 pattern contains line-wrapped character classes, so the JSON is authoritative."\n}\n```'}
