: Brilliant, thank you Mr. Pendelton. Just for data protection and \\r\\nsecurity verification, could you confirm your date of birth and your full UK postcode?\\r\\n[14:31:25] Arthur Pendelton: Certainly. I was born on the 14th of July, 1974, and my \\r\\npostcode is SW1A 1AA.\\r\\n[14:31:50] Agent 512: Splendid, thank you very much for verifying that, Arthur. I\\\'ve located \\r\\nyour account. How can I assist you today?\\r\\n[14:32:10] Arthur Pendelton: I\\\'m calling about an unauthorized direct debit taken from my \\r\\naccount on the 15th of October for £89.50.\\r\\n[14:32:45] Agent 512: I am terribly sorry about that trouble, Arthur. I can see the direct \\r\\ndebit right here. I\\\'ll issue an immediate indemnity claim under the Direct Debit Guarantee \\r\\nand refund the £89.50 back to your account.\\r\\n[14:33:15] Arthur Pendelton: Excellent, thank you. Could you also update my contact mobile \\r\\nnumber on file to +44 7700 900077?\\r\\n[14:33:40] Agent 512: Consider it done, Arthur. I have updated your mobile number to +44 \\r\\n7700 900077 and sent a confirmation text. Anything else I can sort out for you?\\r\\n[14:34:02] Arthur Pendelton: No, that covers everything. Cheers for your help, Oliver.\\r\\n[14:34:15] Agent 512: You\\\'re most welcome, Arthur. Have a lovely afternoon. Cheerio!\\r\\n"""\\r\\n\\r\\n# Detecting PII in the content\\r\\ndetections = []\\r\\nfor classifier in classifiers:\\r\\n    matches = list(re.finditer(classifier[\\\'regex\\\'], content))\\r\\n    for match in matches:\\r\\n        span = match.span(classifier[\\\'group_index\\\']) if classifier[\\\'group_index\\\'] is not None else match.span()\\r\\n        detections.append({\\r\\n            \\\'span\\\': span,\\r\\n            \\\'start\\\': span[0],\\r\\n            \\\'end\\\': span[1],\\r\\n            \\\'length\\\': span[1] - span[0],\\r\\n            \\\'id\\\': classifier[\\\'id\\\'],\\r\\n            \\\'category\\\': classifier[\\\'category\\\'],\\r\\n            \\\'confidence\\\': classifier[\\\'conf\\\'],\\r\\n            \\\'priority\\\': classifier[\\\'priority\\\'],\\r\\n        })\\r\\n\\r\\n# Sorting detections to resolve overlaps\\r\\ndetections.sort(key=lambda x: (x[\\\'start\\\'], -x[\\\'length\\\'], x[\\\'priority\\\'], -x[\\\'confidence\\\']))\\r\\n\\r\\n# Resolving overlaps deterministically (greedy non-overlapping)\\r\\nfinal_spans = []\\r\\nlast_end = -1\\r\\nfor detection in detections:\\r\\n    if detection[\\\'start\\\'] >= last_end:\\r\\n        final_spans.append(detection[\\\'span\\\'])\\r\\n        last_end = detection[\\\'end\\\']\\r\\n\\r\\n# Redacting PII in the file name\\r\\ndef redact_filename(filename):\\r\\n    base, ext = filename.rsplit(\\\'.\\\', 1)\\r\\n    tokens = base.split(\\\'_\\\')\\r\\n    redacted_tokens = ["X" * len(token) if any(re.search(cls[\\\'regex\\\'], token) for cls in classifiers) else token for token in tokens]\\r\\n    return "_".join(redacted_tokens) + \\\'.\\\' + ext\\r\\n\\r\\nredacted_file_name = redact_filename("Arthur_P_Transcription.pdf")\\r\\n\\r\\n# Gathering debug information\\r\\ndebug_info = {\\r\\n    "raw_detections_count": {cls[\\\'category\\\']: 0 for cls in classifiers},\\r\\n    "final_spans": final_spans,\\r\\n}\\r\\n\\r\\n# Counting raw detections per classifier\\r\\nfor det in detections:\\r\\n    debug_info["raw_detections_count"][det[\\\'category\\\']] += 1\\r\\n\\r\\n# Build full JSON\\r\\nfull_json = json.dumps({\\r\\n    "detections": detections,\\r\\n    "final_spans": final_spans,\\r\\n    "redacted_file_name": redacted_file_name,\\r\\n    "debug_info": debug_info,\\r\\n}, indent=2)\\r\\n\\r\\nfull_json\'}, \'extras\': {\'container_id\': \'cntr_6ad632e931d48193929bfa3f675751410a50a6cc4b99a8be\'}}, {\'type\': \'server_tool_result\', \'tool_call_id\': \'ci_04416b06df48e9df006ad632e9efb487d18e73217228c0f758\', \'status\': \'success\'}, {\'type\': \'text\', \'text\': \'Here\\\'s the full JSON output:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  "detections": [\\n    {\\n